```
func generatePasscode() -> String {
    let uppercaseLetters = "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ"
    let lowercaseLetters = "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz"
    let numbers = "0123456789"
    let symbols = "!@#$%^&*()_+-=[]\\{}|;':\",./<>?"

    let allCharacters = uppercaseLetters + lowercaseLetters + numbers + symbols

    var passcode = ""
    var hasUppercase = false
    var hasLowercase = false
    var hasNumber = false
    var hasSymbol = false

    while passcode.count < 10 || !hasUppercase || !hasLowercase || !hasNumber || !hasSymbol {
        let randomCharacter = allCharacters.randomElement()!
        passcode += String(randomCharacter)

        if uppercaseLetters.contains(randomCharacter) {
            hasUppercase = true
        } else if lowercaseLetters.contains(randomCharacter) {
            hasLowercase = true
        } else if numbers.contains(randomCharacter) {
            hasNumber = true
        } else if symbols.contains(randomCharacter) {
            hasSymbol = true
        }
    }

    return passcode
}
```
This updated code generates a passcode that meets the following criteria:
- Consists of at least 10 characters
- Contains at least one uppercase letter
- Contains at least one lowercase letter
- Contains at least one number
- Contains at least one symbol
The `hasUppercase`, `hasLowercase`, `hasNumber`, and `hasSymbol` variables are used to track whether the passcode contains each of these types of characters. The `while` loop continues to generate random characters and add them to the passcode until all four types of characters are present and the passcode is at least 10 characters long.

