What is the most effective way to summarize an essay in Java code? Can you provide a sample code to summarize the essay "The Value of Games and Sport"?
Here's a sample code that uses the TextRank algorithm to summarize the given essay:
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Properties;
import edu.stanford.nlp.pipeline.StanfordCoreNLP;
import edu.stanford.nlp.ling.CoreAnnotations.SentencesAnnotation;
import edu.stanford.nlp.ling.CoreSentence;
import edu.stanford.nlp.ling.CoreAnnotations;
import edu.stanford.nlp.util.ArrayCoreMap;
import edu.stanford.nlp.util.CoreMap;
import edu.stanford.nlp.util.PropertiesUtils;
import edu.stanford.nlp.util.Sets;
import edu.stanford.nlp.ling.tokensregex.CoreMapExpressionExtractor;
import edu.stanford.nlp.ling.tokensregex.CoreMapExpressionExtractor.AnnotatedExpression;
import edu.stanford.nlp.ling.tokensregex.TokenSequencePattern;
import edu.stanford.nlp.ling.tokensregex.matcher.Matcher;
import edu.stanford.nlp.ling.tokensregex.matcher.TokenMatcher;
import edu.stanford.nlp.ling.tokensregex.matcher.TokenPatternMatcher;
import edu.stanford.nlp.process.CoreLabelTokenFactory;
import edu.stanford.nlp.process.PTBTokenizer;
import edu.stanford.nlp.tagger.maxent.MaxentTagger;
import edu.stanford.nlp.trees.Tree;
import edu.stanford.nlp.trees.TreeCoreAnnotations.TreeAnnotation;
import edu.stanford.nlp.trees.TreePrint;
import edu.stanford.nlp.trees.TreeTraverser;
import edu.stanford.nlp.trees.TreeVisitor;
import edu.stanford.nlp.trees.Trees;
public class TextRankSummarizer {
  private static final int MAX_SENTENCES = 5; // Maximum number of sentences to include in summary
  private static final int ITERATIONS = 50; // Number of iterations for TextRank algorithm
  private final StanfordCoreNLP pipeline;
  private final MaxentTagger tagger;
  public TextRankSummarizer() {
    Properties props = PropertiesUtils.asProperties(
        "annotators", "tokenize,ssplit,pos,lemma",
        "ssplit.isOneSentence", "true",
        "tokenize.language", "en",
        "pos.model", "edu/stanford/nlp/models/pos-tagger/english-left3words/english-left3words-distsim.tagger",
        "lemma.model", "edu/stanford/nlp/models/pos-tagger/english-left3words/english-bidirectional-distsim.tagger");
    pipeline = new StanfordCoreNLP(props);
    tagger = new MaxentTagger(props.getProperty("pos.model"));
  }
  public String summarize(String text) {
    List<String> sentences = splitIntoSentences(text);
    List<String> sentenceTokens = tokenizeSentences(sentences);
    List<String> topSentences = getTopSentences(sentenceTokens, MAX_SENTENCES, ITERATIONS);
    return String.join(" ", topSentences);
  }
  private List<String> splitIntoSentences(String text) {
    ArrayCoreMap doc = new ArrayCoreMap();
    doc.set(CoreAnnotations.TextAnnotation.class, text);
    pipeline.annotate(doc);
    List<CoreMap> sentences = doc.get(SentencesAnnotation.class);
    return sentences.stream()
        .map(CoreMap::toString)
        .collect(Collectors.toList());
  }
  private List<String> tokenizeSentences(List<String> sentences) {
    return sentences.stream()
        .map(tagger::tokenize)
        .map(tokens -> String.join(" ", tokens))
        .collect(Collectors.toList());
  }
  private List<String> getTopSentences(List<String> sentences, int maxSentences, int iterations) {
    List<TokenSequencePattern> patterns = getPatterns();
    CoreMapExpressionExtractor extractor = CoreMapExpressionExtractor.createExtractorFromFiles(patterns);
    List<String> topSentences = new ArrayList<>();
    List<AnnotatedExpression> rankedSentences = TextRank.rankSentences(sentences, extractor, maxSentences, iterations);
    for (AnnotatedExpression sentence : rankedSentences) {
      String originalSentence = sentence.getMatchedExpression().toString();
      topSentences.add(originalSentence);
    }
    return topSentences;
  }
  private List<TokenSequencePattern> getPatterns() {
    List<TokenSequencePattern> patterns = new ArrayList<>();
    TokenSequencePattern pattern1 = TokenSequencePattern.compile("({tag:/NN.*|VB.*/}+)"); // Noun or verb phrase
    patterns.add(pattern1);
    TokenSequencePattern pattern2 = TokenSequencePattern.compile("({word:/^not$/i} [{tag:JJ.*}]*)"); // Negation of an adjective
    patterns.add(pattern2);
    TokenSequencePattern pattern3 = TokenSequencePattern.compile("({word:/^not$/i} [{tag:RB.*}]*)"); // Negation of an adverb
    patterns.add(pattern3);
    return patterns;
  }
}
To summarize "The Value of Games and Sport", you can call the summarize() method of the TextRankSummarizer class:
public static void main(String[] args) {
  String essay = "Games and sports are a necessary part of our life. They are to the body what education is to the mind. But, no. They are an integral part of education itself. Those who have not played any games in life should consider their education incomplete. Gandhi greatly lamented for not having given proper attention to games during his formative years. They give us energy and strength. They instill in us a spirit of camaraderie. They sharpen our intellect. They broaden our outlook. They develop in us a sense of discipline. Above all, they keep us fit.";
  TextRankSummarizer summarizer = new TextRankSummarizer();
  String summary = summarizer.summarize(essay);
  System.out.println(summary);
}
